	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[erreurs make]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=27827#p27827"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bonjour,<br />en version 10 sous Linux Oracle<br />Je voulais démarrer avec </p><p>ssl = on<br />Mais j&#039;ai eu l&#039;erreur:<br />SSL is not supported by this build</p><p>Donc j&#039;ai relancé :</p><p>]# ./configure --prefix=/u01/app/PostgreSQL-10 --with-openssl</p><p>Et ensuite <br />#make <br />qui se termine avec:</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>make[3]: *** [libpq.so.5.10] Error 1
make[3]: Leaving directory `/u01/app/postgres/postgresql-10.0/src/interfaces/libpq&#039;
make[2]: *** [all-libpq-recurse] Error 2
make[2]: Leaving directory `/u01/app/postgres/postgresql-10.0/src/interfaces&#039;
make[1]: *** [all-interfaces-recurse] Error 2
make[1]: Leaving directory `/u01/app/postgres/postgresql-10.0/src&#039;
make: *** [all-src-recurse] Error 2</code></pre></div><p>En effet libpq.so.5.10 existe :<br />[root@rac1 ~]# find / -name &quot;libpq.so.5.10&quot;<br />/u01/app/PostgreSQL-10/lib/libpq.so.5.10</p><p>Avez-vous une idée?</p><p>D&#039;avance merci.</p>]]></content>
